# HomeSynapse Core — operator override drop-in.
# Installed to /etc/homesynapse/homesynapse.env (a dpkg conffile — your edits
# survive package upgrades). Loaded by the unit via EnvironmentFile=-.
#
# Every line is KEY=VALUE (no `export`, no shell expansion).

# ── Extra JVM options (appended after the Locked LTD-01 flags) ───────────────
# Honoured by the launcher today. Example: raise the heap on a Standard-tier box.
#HOMESYNAPSE_JVM_OPTS=-Xmx3072m

# ── AppCDS archive (Doc 12 §3.2) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point at a writable path; the launcher auto-creates the shared archive there.
#HOMESYNAPSE_CDS_ARCHIVE=/var/lib/homesynapse/homesynapse.jsa

# ── Runtime base (current artifact) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The unit already sets this; override only for non-standard layouts.
#HOMESYNAPSE_HOME=/var/lib/homesynapse

# ── LAN exposure (NOT yet wired in the current artifact) ────────────────────
# bindHost/httpPort come from HomeSynapseConfig.HOME_DEFAULT today (loopback,
# 7070) and are NOT yet read from env/config — wiring them is Core escalation E2.
# Once E2 lands, the authenticated LAN opt-in will look like:
#   HOMESYNAPSE_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0
#   HOMESYNAPSE_HTTP_PORT=7070
# Until then these keys are inert (documented here so the seam is visible).
